title: 高通胀
subtitle: 工人的购买力正在下降。
view-if: inflation >= 7 and high_inflation_timer = 0 and spd_in_government
new-page: true
on-arrival: capital_strike_progress += 1; hyperinflation += 0.2; workers_spd -= 4; workers_spd += nationalization_progress; old_middle_spd -= 6; new_middle_spd -= 6; rural_spd -= 5; unemployed_spd -= 4; unemployed_spd += welfare; high_inflation_timer = 4 if inflation > 8; high_inflation_timer = 2 if inflation >= 10; pro_republic -= 5; old_middle_nsdap += 2; new_middle_nsdap += 2; rural_nsdap += 2; socialism -= 2
tags: event

= 高通胀

通胀已经上升。各社会阶层的人都眼看着自己的购买力下降。尽管当前的通胀远没有那么严重,1923 年恶性通胀时期的记忆仍在大众意识中回荡。

民众与媒体都在大声呼吁采取行动降低通胀。

- @taxes: 加税。
- @welfare: 削减福利与社会开支。
- @price_controls: 实施价格与工资管制。
- @tighten_controls: 收紧价格与工资管制。
- @bank: 国家银行这次总该有对策了吧?
- @nothing: 现实地说,我们无能为力。

@taxes
on-arrival: upper_tax_rates += 1; lower_tax_rates += 1; budget += 2; unemployed += 1.5; capital_strike_progress -= 1; inflation -= 1; hyperinflation -= 0.2; new_middle_spd -= 3; old_middle_spd -= 3; workers_spd -= 3; rural_spd -= 3; kpd_coalition_dissent += 1; kpd_relation -= 5; left_dissent += 5; economic_growth -= 0.4

加税在所有人中都不受欢迎,但这或许正是控制通货膨胀所必需的。

@welfare
on-arrival: welfare -= 1; budget += 1; capital_strike_progress -= 2; unemployed += 1.5; new_middle_spd += 4*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 4*(1-dissent); workers_spd -= 5; unemployed_spd -= 5; inflation -= 1; hyperinflation -= 0.2; left_dissent += 5; labor_dissent += 5; center_dissent += 5; kpd_coalition_dissent += 1; economic_growth -= 0.4

依古典经济学,削减政府开支应当能降低通货膨胀率。但这会把痛苦加诸最受苦的人身上。

@price_controls
view-if: not price_controls
on-arrival: price_controls = 1; black_market += 3; black_market += 6 if capital_strike_seen; inflation_goal = 5; capital_strike_progress += 3; inflation -= 3; hyperinflation = 0; coalition_dissent += 1; unemployed += 1; old_middle_spd -= 4; new_middle_spd -= 3; rural_spd -= 5; workers_spd -= 2; unemployed_spd += 3; labor_dissent += 6; dvp_relation -= 6; z_relation -= 4; ddp_relation -= 4; economic_growth -= 0.4

价格管制在资产阶级及其代表以及农村生产者中极不受欢迎,而工资管制则伤害有组织的工人。不过,这些政策至少多少遏制了通胀的势头。

@tighten_controls
view-if: price_controls
on-arrival: inflation_goal -= 1 if inflation_goal > price_controls; capital_strike_progress += 2; inflation -= 2; black_market += 6; hyperinflation = 0; coalition_dissent += 1; unemployed += 1; old_middle_spd -= 2; new_middle_spd -= 2; rural_spd -= 4; workers_spd -= 1; unemployed_spd += 2; labor_dissent += 3; dvp_relation -= 3; z_relation -= 2; ddp_relation -= 2; economic_growth -= 0.2

We tighten price controls, aiming to reduce inflation further beyond its current levels. This causes further growth in the black market.

@bank
on-arrival: capital_strike_progress += 2

Unfortunately, but perhaps expectedly, the Reichsbank is refusing to help the government, claiming that our socialist policies are solely to blame. Reichsbank president [? if year <= 1930 : Hjalmar Schacht ?][? if year > 1930 : Hans Luther ?] is all but calling for the fall of the government.

@nothing
on-arrival: capital_strike_progress += 1

现实地说,我们无法遏止通货膨胀的浪潮。

